3 1 DeclarationofPurpose.
4 I. The general court finds and affirms that parents have a fundamental liberty interest to
5 raise and care for their minor children, as well as make decisions concerning their care and custody,
6 and this fundamental liberty interest is protected under both the federal and New Hampshire
7 constitutions.
8 II. The general court further finds that it is a child’s parents who have the responsibility,
9 means, and resources to ensure that a child receives appropriate health care, social support,
10 religiousguidance,andmoralinculcationtodevelopintohappyandproductivemembersofsociety.
11 III. Accordingly, the general court further finds that parents have the right to access, be
12 notified of, and be provided with all information relating to these rights, and that it is necessary to
13 establish a consistent mechanism for parents to be notified of information relating to the health,
14 well-being, and educational progress of their minor children while those children are in the custody
15 andcontrolofaschool.
